      "id": "lightning",
      "title": "Lightning",
      "description": "Where lightning was seen from the International Space Station (NASA's LIS instrument), month by month from January 2017 to July 2023. Each frame shows only its own month, nothing accumulated, so the storm belt moves north and south with the seasons. Brighter means lightning in more of the ten-day windows of that month; it is a relative frequency read from a NASA visualization, not a flash count. LIS sees only between about 55° N and 55° S.",
      "source": {
        "title": "Lightning Events Detected from the ISS 2017-2023 (NASA SVS 5011)",
        "url": "https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/5011"
      },
